.TH PEISO 1 2026-11-10 "Peios peiso 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
peiso \- build bootable Peios ISOs from ppk packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peiso resolve
.I spec
.br
.B peiso build
.RB [ \-\-mkirf
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-mkuki
.IR file ]
.B \-\-out
.I file spec
.br
.B peiso
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peiso
builds an ISO that boots a Peios live system under UEFI, from the
packages a spec names.
.PP
It resolves the packages the spec names with
.BR ppk (1)'s
resolver, choosing from the spec's repositories one version of each
package they depend on or require, and copies every package chosen into
the ISO's own store, checking each as
.BR ppk (1)
fetches it.
It composes the initramfs from the packages the spec puts there, with
prelude as its init and the identifier of its medium as
.IR /system/medium ,
and packs it with
.BR mkirf .
.B mkuki
then makes the initramfs, the kernel and its command line into a unified
kernel image, which
.B peiso
places as the loader of an EFI system partition image.
The ISO holds that image, as its UEFI boot image, and:
.TP
.I /artifacts
The store, holding every package chosen.
.TP
.I /live.toml
The live system's environment profile.
.TP
.I /peios-medium
The medium's identifier, the SHA-256 hash of the packages and the profile,
so that the same spec and packages always make the same medium.
.PP
At boot, prelude runs the live-root hook, which finds the ISO by its
identifier on whichever disk, disc or stick it is attached as, and
composes the live system from its profile and store, on a tmpfs.
The initramfs therefore needs what the hook runs, such as
.B ppk
and a shell, as well as prelude and the hook.
.SH THE SPEC
A spec is a TOML file.
Paths in it are relative to its directory.
.PP
.RS
.EX
disable_default_repos = true

[[repository]]
filepath = "artifacts"

[kernel]
file = "vmlinuz"
cmdline = "console=ttyS0 rd.shell"

[[package]]
name = "net.busybox.busybox"
initramfs = true

[[package]]
name = "dev.peios.prelude"
liveboot = false
initramfs = true
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B edition
The Peios edition the live system is, such as
.BR Experimental .
Its package is
.B dev.peios.peios\-
followed by the edition in lowercase.
.TP
.B edition_package
The package of an edition that is not one of Peios's own, in place of
.BR edition .
.TP
.B version
The edition package's version, as for a
.BR [[package]] .
.TP
.B disable_default_repos
Whether to leave out the default repository, pkgs.peios.org.
It is not available yet, so this must be
.BR true .
.TP
.B [[repository]]
A place packages come from:
.B filepath
names an artifact directory.
A package is taken from the first repository, in the order given, that
holds the version chosen.
Repositories must agree on what each version of a package is.
.TP
.B [kernel]
The kernel the ISO boots, and its command line,
.BR cmdline ,
empty by default.
The kernel is either a
.BR file ,
or a
.BR package ,
with an optional
.BR version ,
whose image is at
.IR usr/lib/modules/vmlinuz .
The ISO carries a kernel package in its store, and a
.B [[package]]
naming it says where else it goes.
.TP
.B [[package]]
A package the ISO carries:
.B name
and
.BR version ,
a version constraint such as
.BR ">= 1.2" ,
in which a version on its own is that version exactly.
The newest version that will do, for the host's architecture, is carried.
.B liveboot
puts the package, and everything it needs, in the live system, and is
.B true
by default.
.B initramfs
puts it, and everything it needs, in the initramfs, and is
.B false
by default.
A package that is in neither is carried in the ISO's store only, for
fetching from later.
.TP
.B [initramfs]
What the initramfs holds outside
.IR usr ,
as an environment profile's
.B symlinks
and
.B dirs
give it.
By default
.I init
links to
.IR usr/sbin/prelude ,
with empty
.IR proc ,
.IR sys ,
and
.IR tmp .
A table given replaces the default.
.TP
.B [liveboot]
What the live system holds outside
.IR usr ,
in the same way.
By default
.I bin
and
.I sbin
link to
.I usr/bin
and
.IR usr/sbin ,
with an empty
.IR tmp .
.PP
The edition's package, the kernel package and every
.B [[package]]
are resolved together, so the store holds one version of each package.
The live system holds the edition, each package with
.BR liveboot ,
and everything they depend on or require; the initramfs holds each
package with
.B initramfs
and everything it needs, at the versions the store holds.
A dependency goes where the package that needs it goes, and nowhere else,
so a package meant for the initramfs must be placed there.
.PP
Some keys are understood but refused until what they need exists:
.B url
in a repository until repositories on the network, and
.B autoinstall
and
.B offerinstall
until an installer.
Any other key is an error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI resolve " spec"
Print each package the ISO
.I spec
describes would carry, one to a line: the package, where it goes
.RB ( liveboot ,
.BR initramfs ,
both, or
.B store
for the store only), and, in parentheses, what first asked for it.
.TP
.BI build " spec"
Build the ISO
.I spec
describes and print its path.
It is built in a directory beside it, which is removed afterwards, and
renamed into place whole.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-out " file"
Write the ISO to
.IR file ,
replacing any there.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-mkirf " file"
Pack the initramfs with this
.BR mkirf ,
rather than the one on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-mkuki " file"
Make the unified kernel image with this
.BR mkuki ,
rather than the one on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including printing help or the version.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, such as a spec with errors, a package or a dependency that no
repository holds at a version that will do, a package that fails its
checks, or a tool that fails.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an unknown option or a missing argument.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B peiso
runs
.BR mkfs.vfat ,
.BR mmd ,
.BR mcopy ,
and
.B xorriso
from
.BR PATH .
None needs privilege.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppk (1),
.BR pekit (1),
.BR mkirf (1),
.BR mkuki (1)
